-- title:
--   Rank of the Cartier module equals the height
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $k$ be a perfect field of characteristic $p$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$ in the sense of the project structure [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalModule.html#L170): a two-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ over $k$ (a pair of power series in $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,2$ variables with vanishing constant terms, normalised linear terms and associative), together with the assertion that $X.F$ is commutative, an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ and a uniformising endomorphism $\varpi$ by pairs of power series that are endomorphisms of $X.F$, subject to the usual relations ($\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = a^{\sigma}\circ\varpi$). Let $b$ be a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,4$, over the Witt vectors $W(k)$, of the Cartier module [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule p X.F`](def/MvFormalGroup_CartierModule.html#L162), whose elements are pairs of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathbb N$ with zero constant term which are additive for the Witt addition law with respect to $X.F$. Let $h$ be a natural number such that the $k$-dimension of $k[[x_1,x_2]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the two components of the $p$-fold iterate $X.F.nthSeries\ p$ (the multiplication-by-$p$ series of $X.F$, defined by iterating $\Phi \mapsto F(\Phi, x)$ from $0$) equals $p^h$. Then $h = 4$.
--
--   This is the counting step in the identification of the rank of the Cartier–Dieudonné module of a formal group over a perfect field with its height: a $W(k)$-basis of four elements is incompatible with a kernel of multiplication by $p$ of order other than $p^4$. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.hasHeight_four_of_basis_cartierModule_of_X_pow_mem_span`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.hasHeight_four_of_basis_cartierModule_of_X_pow_mem_span), on the way to showing that the special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules occurring in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation have height $4$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_eq_four_of_basis_cartierModule_of_finrank_eq_pow.lean

